url: "https://github.com/QingjingChen/Heart"
abstract: >
  HEART is an interactive audit-and-repair toolkit for existing AI-ethics
  benchmarks. It treats each benchmark as a bundle of reusable tools
  (dataset patterns, task formats, metrics, evaluator protocols, governance
  practices). The resource bundles together: (a) a meta-review of 103
  benchmarks across 5 ethical dimensions cross-walked to 16
  policy/governance sources; (b) a 14-rubric diagnostic codebook with
  v2 calibrated anchors, expert-validated across all 103 benchmarks; (c) a
  two-layer workbox of 14 generic repair tools plus 103 specific repair
  sub-tools (one per audited bench); (d) a 4-step
  audit-diagnosis-prescription-revision guidebook; and (e) an interactive
  site that walks through the full workflow in the browser.
keywords:
